  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Value Chain Development Kurdistan region of the Republic of Iraq</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iraq holds the fifth largest economy in the Middle East, which is starting to open up to foreign business due to increasing stability. The Iraqi government aims to greatly diversify its economy and create economic sustainability and desires to attract more foreign businesses.  The Netherlands already has a strong agricultural reputation and a vast network within the Kurdish Region of Iraq that enables Dutch companies to trade and collaborate. During a high-level visit from the Kurdish region of Iraq in June 2025, a business forum will be organised. The aim of the business forum is to provide a platform for companies from the Netherlands and the Kurdistan Region of Iraq to meet and potentially reach further agreements on cooperation/trade.</narrative>
  </description>
